                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/incompleteness+theorem"} incompleteness theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L%C3%B6b%27s+theorem"} Löb's theorem
          %h2#References References
          %p The original article:
          %ul
            %li#Lawvere69
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Diagonal Arguments and Cartesian Closed Categories
              %strong 92
              (1969) 134-145 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/15/tr15abs.html"}> tac:15
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Review and further development:
          %ul
            %li#Yanofsky03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noson+Yanofsky"}> Noson Yanofsky
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Universal Approach to Self-Referential Paradoxes, Incompleteness and Fixed Points
              %strong 9
              3 (2003) 362-386 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0305282"}> arXiv:math/0305282
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/3109884"} jstor:3109884
          %p Exposition:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"}> Andrej Bauer
              ,
              %em On a proof of Cantor’s theorem
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.andrej.com/2007/04/08/on-a-proof-of-cantors-theorem/"}> web
              )
          %p
            Formalization in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
          %ul
            %li#Escardo18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Escardo"}> Martin Escardo
              ,
              %em On Lawvere’s Fixed Point Theorem
              (2018) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~mhe/agda-new/LawvereFPT.html"}> agda development
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p The necessary assumptions for Lawvere’s account are reduced in various ways in
          %ul
            %li#Roberts
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Michael+Roberts"}> David Michael Roberts
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Substructural fixed-point theorems and the diagonal argument: theme and variations
              %strong 5
              issue 8 (2023) doi:
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.32408/compositionality-5-8"}> 10.32408/compositionality-5-8
              ,
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.00239"}> arXiv:2110.00239
                ).
